    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0098" n="56" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg56"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Sprague.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Klingendan’s name throws much suspicion on the sale. You must refuse to recognize
                    it. And if the Sumter try to slip off under a British flag, Captain Bryson must
                    stop and take her on the high seas if he can. He need not mind the twenty-four
                    hour rule, if outside the jurisdiction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES F. ADAMS, <hi rendition="#italic">United States Minister,
                            London.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sprague</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">United
                            States Consul, Gibraltar.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
